{
  "headline": "Every device×geo×destination cut for coupons is too thin to declare a real winner — all 316 apply-rate segments, 541 code/segment mixes, and 252 reject-reason rows sit at n<50 — but within that limit, EXPIRED5 is the one code showing up repeatedly among the worst-rejected across multiple segments and reasons.",
  "whatsHappening": "Overall, apply rate is 27.6% (n=2,100) and among entered codes 68.4% validate vs 31.6% rejected (n=848), split across about 6 coupon codes, 4 device types, 7 countries and 14 destinations. EXPIRED5 appears three separate times in the highest reject-count rows — already_used (ios/IN/EG, 3), invalid_code (android/IN/FR, 3), and min_cart_not_met (web-user-b2c/IN/AU, 2) — while ATLYS15 shows one comparable spike (already_used, android/IN/SG, 3) and FREESHIP one (already_used, android/IN/US, 2).",
  "whyItHappens": "EXPIRED5's rejections span three different reasons (already_used, invalid_code, min_cart_not_met) across three unrelated segments rather than clustering in one device or geo — that pattern points to the code itself (naming/expiry logic) being the driver, not a segment-specific friction point.",
  "evidence": {
    "title": "Top reject-count rows by code/reason/segment · coupon_rejected, all 252 rows, unfiltered",
    "chart": {
