        ["ATLYS15", "already_used", "android", "IN", "SG", 3],
        ["EXPIRED5", "invalid_code", "android", "IN", "FR", 3],
        ["EXPIRED5", "min_cart_not_met", "web-user-b2c", "IN", "AU", 2],
        ["FREESHIP", "already_used", "android", "IN", "US", 2]
      ]
    }
  },
  "groundedInContext": "Known issue (K6 v1): a SUMMER20 promo ran in Q2 with expected elevated activity — any SUMMER20 segment reads should account for that campaign timing rather than being taken as steady-state. Separately, every one of the three tasks here is gate-flagged low confidence (all sample sizes under 50), so no single device/geo/destination/code cell should be treated as a settled result.",
  "recommendedAction": "Don't ship per-segment code targeting off this data — the cells are too sparse (n<50 everywhere). Instead, pull a longer window or larger sample focused on EXPIRED5's rejection logic specifically (it's the only code hitting multiple reject reasons across unrelated segments), and re-run this same segment cut once volume is sufficient per device×geo×destination cell."
